From 321fef65485841086f0edef0597be47a1d632a43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:08:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: leave the GUI pass out of Dolby Vision frames
 where no control is dirty

Kodi leaves the GUI pass out of a frame when no control marked itself dirty, but
only where the video has a plane of its own (IsRenderingVideoLayer()): with the
video drawn by the render pass, the video window and its control mark themselves
dirty in every frame so that the pass that draws the picture keeps running.
Native Dolby Vision output draws the picture in RenderEx(), after the GUI pass,
and puts the GUI over it from its FBO (CompositeGui()). The FBO of the frame
before is what drawing the GUI again would put in it wherever nothing dirtied
itself, so the walk of every control and its draw calls (on a GPU that is also
doing the packing) can go, with the same bytes sent to the display.

GuiPassReusable() is pure and decides from CDVGuiReuse: setting
(<video><dvguireuse>, on by default), native output, a composited GUI, an FBO of
the output's size that a drawn frame has been composited into, no menus in Dolby
Vision, no partial redraws, no stereoscopic mode, and no subtitles or debug
information over the picture (they are not left to the dirty regions alone).
Captures mark the window manager dirty themselves. A frame whose pass was left
out takes whether the GUI was empty from m_guiFboClean (set from the count of
the frame that drew it, so a clean flag means the count was zero), keeps the
direct way for it, and counts as composed otherwise; the view of the renderer is
updated by RenderManager in that frame, since the GUI pass is what did it. An
FBO made after the decision is cleared and the next frame draws.

The 10 s line of Dolby Vision says what the composed frames had over the
picture (GUI elements, of them how many from the FBO of the frame before,
subtitles or debug alone, a capture) and the window on top; the reason that the
pass is drawn is logged once, and again when it changes.

Host test (outside the tree): dvguireuse_test, every fact on its own in both directions.
